    "title": "Problem 6898",
    "description": "Write a Python function called `interleave_queues_1` that must interleave two queues and append marker 1. Practice stacks & queues.\nDifficulty: Expert.\nExamples:\n  interleave_queues_1([1, 3], [2, 4]) -> [1, 2, 3, 4, 1]\n  interleave_queues_1([1], [2, 3]) -> [1, 2, 3, 1]",
    "initialCode": "from collections import deque\n\ndef interleave_queues_1(left, right):\n    pass",
    "solution": "from collections import deque\n\n# Example 1: canonical function approach\ndef interleave_queues_1(left, right):\n    first = deque(left)\n    second = deque(right)\n    result = []\n    while first or second:\n        if first:\n            result.append(first.popleft())\n        if second:\n            result.append(second.popleft())\n    result.append(1)\n    return result\n\nprint(interleave_queues_1([1, 3], [2, 4]))  # Expected: [1, 2, 3, 4, 1]\nprint(interleave_queues_1([1], [2, 3]))  # Expected: [1, 2, 3, 1]\n\n# Example 2: nested helper approach\ndef solve_problem_6898(left, right):\n    def calculate():\n        first = deque(left)\n        second = deque(right)\n        result = []\n        while first or second:\n            if first:\n                result.append(first.popleft())\n            if second:\n                result.append(second.popleft())\n        result.append(1)\n        return result\n    return calculate()\n\nprint(solve_problem_6898([1, 3], [2, 4]))\n\n# Example 3: static method approach\nclass Problem6898Solution:\n    @staticmethod\n    def interleave_queues_1(left, right):\n        first = deque(left)\n        second = deque(right)\n        result = []\n        while first or second:\n            if first:\n                result.append(first.popleft())\n            if second:\n                result.append(second.popleft())\n        result.append(1)\n        return result\n\nprint(Problem6898Solution.interleave_queues_1([1], [2, 3]))\n\n# Example 4: assigned result approach\nresult = interleave_queues_1([1, 3], [2, 4])\nprint(result)\n\n# Example 5: boundary case\nprint(interleave_queues_1([], []))",
    "hint": "Focus on LIFO and FIFO ordering, push/pop operations, deque operations, and safe empty-container behavior. Work from the input types and required behavior instead of copying an example output.",
