    "id": 6903,
    "title": "Problem 6903",
    "description": "Write a Python function called `queue_last_after_1` that must enqueue 1, dequeue one item when possible, and return the final queue. Practice stacks & queues.\nDifficulty: Expert.\nExamples:\n  queue_last_after_1([1, 2]) -> [2, 1]\n  queue_last_after_1([]) -> []",
