    "description": "Write a Python function called `csv_select_rows_4` that must return CSV rows whose named column equals expected, plus marker row 4. Practice csv & json.\nDifficulty: Intermediate.\nExamples:\n  csv_select_rows_4(\"name,role\\nAda,dev\\nBob,test\", \"role\", \"dev\") -> [{\"name\": \"Ada\", \"role\": \"dev\"}, {\"marker\": \"4\"}]\n  csv_select_rows_4(\"x\\n1\", \"x\", \"9\") -> [{\"marker\": \"4\"}]",
    "initialCode": "import csv\nfrom io import StringIO\n\ndef csv_select_rows_4(text, column, expected):\n    pass",
    "solution": "import csv\nfrom io import StringIO\n\n# Example 1: canonical function approach\ndef csv_select_rows_4(text, column, expected):\n    rows = csv.DictReader(StringIO(text))\n    result = [dict(row) for row in rows if row[column] == expected]\n    result.append({\"marker\": str(4)})\n    return result\n\nprint(csv_select_rows_4(\"name,role\\nAda,dev\\nBob,test\", \"role\", \"dev\"))  # Expected: [{\"name\": \"Ada\", \"role\": \"dev\"}, {\"marker\": \"4\"}]\nprint(csv_select_rows_4(\"x\\n1\", \"x\", \"9\"))  # Expected: [{\"marker\": \"4\"}]\n\n# Example 2: nested helper approach\ndef solve_problem_7031(text, column, expected):\n    def calculate():\n        rows = csv.DictReader(StringIO(text))\n        result = [dict(row) for row in rows if row[column] == expected]\n        result.append({\"marker\": str(4)})\n        return result\n    return calculate()\n\nprint(solve_problem_7031(\"name,role\\nAda,dev\\nBob,test\", \"role\", \"dev\"))\n\n# Example 3: static method approach\nclass Problem7031Solution:\n    @staticmethod\n    def csv_select_rows_4(text, column, expected):\n        rows = csv.DictReader(StringIO(text))\n        result = [dict(row) for row in rows if row[column] == expected]\n        result.append({\"marker\": str(4)})\n        return result\n\nprint(Problem7031Solution.csv_select_rows_4(\"x\\n1\", \"x\", \"9\"))\n\n# Example 4: assigned result approach\nresult = csv_select_rows_4(\"name,role\\nAda,dev\\nBob,test\", \"role\", \"dev\")\nprint(result)\n\n# Example 5: boundary case\nprint(csv_select_rows_4(\"a,b\\n\", \"a\", \"x\"))",
