    "description": "Write a Python function called `merge_sorted_1` that must merge two sorted lists and append 1. Practice algorithms & complexity.\nDifficulty: Easy.\nExamples:\n  merge_sorted_1([1, 3], [2, 4]) -> [1, 2, 3, 4, 1]\n  merge_sorted_1([], [1]) -> [1, 1]",
    "initialCode": "def merge_sorted_1(left, right):\n    pass",
    "solution": "# Example 1: canonical function approach\ndef merge_sorted_1(left, right):\n    result = []\n    i = j = 0\n    while i < len(left) and j < len(right):\n        if left[i] <= right[j]:\n            result.append(left[i])\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            result.append(right[j])\n            j += 1\n    result.extend(left[i:])\n    result.extend(right[j:])\n    result.append(1)\n    return result\n\nprint(merge_sorted_1([1, 3], [2, 4]))  # Expected: [1, 2, 3, 4, 1]\nprint(merge_sorted_1([], [1]))  # Expected: [1, 1]\n\n# Example 2: nested helper approach\ndef solve_problem_7073(left, right):\n    def calculate():\n        result = []\n        i = j = 0\n        while i < len(left) and j < len(right):\n            if left[i] <= right[j]:\n                result.append(left[i])\n                i += 1\n            else:\n                result.append(right[j])\n                j += 1\n        result.extend(left[i:])\n        result.extend(right[j:])\n        result.append(1)\n        return result\n    return calculate()\n\nprint(solve_problem_7073([1, 3], [2, 4]))\n\n# Example 3: static method approach\nclass Problem7073Solution:\n    @staticmethod\n    def merge_sorted_1(left, right):\n        result = []\n        i = j = 0\n        while i < len(left) and j < len(right):\n            if left[i] <= right[j]:\n                result.append(left[i])\n                i += 1\n            else:\n                result.append(right[j])\n                j += 1\n        result.extend(left[i:])\n        result.extend(right[j:])\n        result.append(1)\n        return result\n\nprint(Problem7073Solution.merge_sorted_1([], [1]))\n\n# Example 4: assigned result approach\nresult = merge_sorted_1([1, 3], [2, 4])\nprint(result)\n\n# Example 5: boundary case\nprint(merge_sorted_1([-2, 5], [-1, 6]))",
