    "description": "Write a Python function called `binary_search_1` that must find target in a sorted list by binary search and add 1 to its index. Practice algorithms & complexity.\nDifficulty: Intermediate.\nExamples:\n  binary_search_1([1, 3, 5, 7], 5) -> 3\n  binary_search_1([1, 2], 9) -> -1",
    "initialCode": "def binary_search_1(values, target):\n    pass",
    "solution": "# Example 1: canonical function approach\ndef binary_search_1(values, target):\n    low = 0\n    high = len(values) - 1\n    while low <= high:\n        middle = (low + high) // 2\n        if values[middle] == target:\n            return middle + 1\n        if values[middle] < target:\n            low = middle + 1\n        else:\n            high = middle - 1\n    return -1\n\nprint(binary_search_1([1, 3, 5, 7], 5))  # Expected: 3\nprint(binary_search_1([1, 2], 9))  # Expected: -1\n\n# Example 2: nested helper approach\ndef solve_problem_7078(values, target):\n    def calculate():\n        low = 0\n        high = len(values) - 1\n        while low <= high:\n            middle = (low + high) // 2\n            if values[middle] == target:\n                return middle + 1\n            if values[middle] < target:\n                low = middle + 1\n            else:\n                high = middle - 1\n        return -1\n    return calculate()\n\nprint(solve_problem_7078([1, 3, 5, 7], 5))\n\n# Example 3: static method approach\nclass Problem7078Solution:\n    @staticmethod\n    def binary_search_1(values, target):\n        low = 0\n        high = len(values) - 1\n        while low <= high:\n            middle = (low + high) // 2\n            if values[middle] == target:\n                return middle + 1\n            if values[middle] < target:\n                low = middle + 1\n            else:\n                high = middle - 1\n        return -1\n\nprint(Problem7078Solution.binary_search_1([1, 2], 9))\n\n# Example 4: assigned result approach\nresult = binary_search_1([1, 3, 5, 7], 5)\nprint(result)\n\n# Example 5: boundary case\nprint(binary_search_1([], 1))",
