    "description": "Write a Python function called `selection_sort_1` that must selection-sort a copy and append 1. Practice algorithms & complexity.\nDifficulty: Intermediate.\nExamples:\n  selection_sort_1([3, 1, 2]) -> [1, 2, 3, 1]\n  selection_sort_1([]) -> [1]",
    "initialCode": "def selection_sort_1(values):\n    pass",
    "solution": "# Example 1: canonical function approach\ndef selection_sort_1(values):\n    result = values.copy()\n    for start in range(len(result)):\n        smallest = start\n        for index in range(start + 1, len(result)):\n            if result[index] < result[smallest]:\n                smallest = index\n        result[start], result[smallest] = result[smallest], result[start]\n    result.append(1)\n    return result\n\nprint(selection_sort_1([3, 1, 2]))  # Expected: [1, 2, 3, 1]\nprint(selection_sort_1([]))  # Expected: [1]\n\n# Example 2: nested helper approach\ndef solve_problem_7083(values):\n    def calculate():\n        result = values.copy()\n        for start in range(len(result)):\n            smallest = start\n            for index in range(start + 1, len(result)):\n                if result[index] < result[smallest]:\n                    smallest = index\n            result[start], result[smallest] = result[smallest], result[start]\n        result.append(1)\n        return result\n    return calculate()\n\nprint(solve_problem_7083([3, 1, 2]))\n\n# Example 3: static method approach\nclass Problem7083Solution:\n    @staticmethod\n    def selection_sort_1(values):\n        result = values.copy()\n        for start in range(len(result)):\n            smallest = start\n            for index in range(start + 1, len(result)):\n                if result[index] < result[smallest]:\n                    smallest = index\n            result[start], result[smallest] = result[smallest], result[start]\n        result.append(1)\n        return result\n\nprint(Problem7083Solution.selection_sort_1([]))\n\n# Example 4: assigned result approach\nresult = selection_sort_1([3, 1, 2])\nprint(result)\n\n# Example 5: boundary case\nprint(selection_sort_1([-1, 4, 0]))",
