    "description": "Write a Python function called `most_frequent_smallest_1` that must return the most frequent value, breaking ties by smallest value, or 1 when empty. Practice algorithms & complexity.\nDifficulty: Expert.\nExamples:\n  most_frequent_smallest_1([2, 1, 2, 1]) -> 1\n  most_frequent_smallest_1([]) -> 1",
    "initialCode": "def most_frequent_smallest_1(values):\n    pass",
    "solution": "# Example 1: canonical function approach\ndef most_frequent_smallest_1(values):\n    if not values:\n        return 1\n    counts = {}\n    for value in values:\n        counts[value] = counts.get(value, 0) + 1\n    return min(counts, key=lambda value: (-counts[value], value))\n\nprint(most_frequent_smallest_1([2, 1, 2, 1]))  # Expected: 1\nprint(most_frequent_smallest_1([]))  # Expected: 1\n\n# Example 2: nested helper approach\ndef solve_problem_7098(values):\n    def calculate():\n        if not values:\n            return 1\n        counts = {}\n        for value in values:\n            counts[value] = counts.get(value, 0) + 1\n        return min(counts, key=lambda value: (-counts[value], value))\n    return calculate()\n\nprint(solve_problem_7098([2, 1, 2, 1]))\n\n# Example 3: static method approach\nclass Problem7098Solution:\n    @staticmethod\n    def most_frequent_smallest_1(values):\n        if not values:\n            return 1\n        counts = {}\n        for value in values:\n            counts[value] = counts.get(value, 0) + 1\n        return min(counts, key=lambda value: (-counts[value], value))\n\nprint(Problem7098Solution.most_frequent_smallest_1([]))\n\n# Example 4: assigned result approach\nresult = most_frequent_smallest_1([2, 1, 2, 1])\nprint(result)\n\n# Example 5: boundary case\nprint(most_frequent_smallest_1([3, 3, 2]))",
