    "title": "Problem 7103",
    "description": "Write a Python function called `rotate_left_1` that must rotate a list left by 1 positions in linear time. Practice algorithms & complexity.\nDifficulty: Expert.\nExamples:\n  rotate_left_1([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]) -> [2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 1]\n  rotate_left_1([]) -> []",
    "initialCode": "def rotate_left_1(values):\n    pass",
    "solution": "# Example 1: canonical function approach\ndef rotate_left_1(values):\n    if not values:\n        return []\n    shift = 1 % len(values)\n    return values[shift:] + values[:shift]\n\nprint(rotate_left_1([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]))  # Expected: [2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 1]\nprint(rotate_left_1([]))  # Expected: []\n\n# Example 2: nested helper approach\ndef solve_problem_7103(values):\n    def calculate():\n        if not values:\n            return []\n        shift = 1 % len(values)\n        return values[shift:] + values[:shift]\n    return calculate()\n\nprint(solve_problem_7103([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]))\n\n# Example 3: static method approach\nclass Problem7103Solution:\n    @staticmethod\n    def rotate_left_1(values):\n        if not values:\n            return []\n        shift = 1 % len(values)\n        return values[shift:] + values[:shift]\n\nprint(Problem7103Solution.rotate_left_1([]))\n\n# Example 4: assigned result approach\nresult = rotate_left_1([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6])\nprint(result)\n\n# Example 5: boundary case\nprint(rotate_left_1([9]))",
